{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T21:14:02.437Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a4268fe12c2a5f9fcd4da8d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1642"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1642: brief pm list and pm search pages print an envelope as large as their rows; the default sort and search's default omission receipt are no longer compacted"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1642\n\nReproduced on the current source build (2026.10.31). pm list: projectPmBriefListEnvelope (src/sdk/output/list-envelope.ts, pm-6pycus) only drops the default sorting block when it has exactly the keys sort and order. Sorting later gained effective_keys, so the 7-line default sort is printed on every brief list page — the compaction silently stopped matching its own default. filters echoes limit, which applied_limit already states. pm search has no brief projection at all: it prints truncated (equal to has_more), filters {limit} (equal to applied_limit) and a 4-line omission_receipt whose only group is projection_metadata restorable with --full.\n\nDeliberate exclusions, with reasons: completeness unchecked stays visible (pm-6pycus AC: unchecked and partial source evidence cannot become complete or disappear); the items_encoding block stays because it is the lossless decode contract for the matched_fields list column, and the formatter round-trip tests require json_columns and absent to restore rows; JSON, --full and SDK result types keep the full receipts.\n\nDuplicate search: 'brief envelope list', GH-1501, GH-1642; nearest is pm-6pycus (GH-1501 brief list envelope, closed) which this extends."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","github","output","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-31T21:14:02.437Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T21:14:02.437Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A default brief pm list page omits the default sorting block including effective_keys and a filters.limit equal to applied_limit; a default pm search page omits truncated when equal to has_more, a filters block that only echoes applied_limit, and replaces the single default projection_metadata omission receipt with details --full; unchecked or partial completeness, non-default sorting, non-limit filters, custom omission receipts, JSON, --full and SDK results are unchanged; the search projection is a reusable SDK export that leaves its input unchanged; measured envelope bytes drop on a small page"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Small default pm list and pm search pages print only envelope fields that carry information, while JSON, --full and SDK results keep complete receipts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-6pycus","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-31T21:14:02.437Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1627","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-31T21:14:02.437Z","author":"harness:claude-code","so