{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-31T21:49:41.856Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8a4268fe12c2a5f9fcd4da8d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1642","claim:pm-gh1643","claim:pm-gh1644","claim:pm-hke9z7","lineage:pm-hke9z7","lineage:pm-5k4v","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1642+pm-gh1643+pm-gh1644+pm-hke9z7","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1642","claim:pm-gh1643","claim:pm-gh1644","claim:pm-hke9z7","lineage:pm-hke9z7","lineage:pm-5k4v","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.314","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-31T21:49:41.855Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Design correction while testing: the 7-line default sort block is not only redundant metadata. GH-1507's accepted contract (pm-zd46m7, integration spec default-list-order) requires brief TOON to disclose the effective default comparator order so an agent knows why rows arrive in that order. Dropping it would undo that decision. The projection therefore drops only the legacy sort/order echo and renders the effective keys on one line, for example sorting.effective_keys 'status_registry:nonterminal_before_terminal asc, priority asc, updated_at desc, id asc'. Seven lines become two, and JSON keeps the full pair array. A malformed or extended sorting block passes through unchanged."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-31T21:49:41.856Z"}],"before_hash":"62d50ec868bfec0715884b79ab47980e777ed5dc1402be7478fc6fb48daad7e4","after_hash":"51547f15e4c4b3baed63e1ff60d34e6c6d913373aed163b